{# Everything this provider holds about the signed-in person, in one file they ask for (RGPD articles 15
   and 20, issue #453), in the language of the browser: what the file holds, where their last request has
   got to, and the button that asks for one. The five states are one page and never an empty one: a person
   who clicked learns whether their file is being built, waiting for them, gone, or being built by nobody.
   A file that is ready leaves in one of two forms, and a request goes away on the word of the person it
   is of in whatever state it is in, before the date it would have gone away on by itself. #}
{% extends '@Beffroi/layout.html.twig' %}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}

{% block title %}{{ 'archive.title'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{# Asking for the file is what this page offers, so it is read beside the title and not under everything
   the page says. Asking again replaces what is there, so the one state with no button is the one being
   built: there is nothing a second click would do but queue the same work twice. A build that did not
   come back is not that state, and the button is back: what it replaces is a row nobody is filling. #}
{% block action %}
    {% if state != 'being_built' %}
        <form method="post" action="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account_archive_ask') }}" data-archive-ask>
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('beffroi_archive_ask') }}">
            <button type="submit">{{ (state == 'never' ? 'archive.ask' : 'archive.ask_again')|trans }}</button>
        </form>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    {{ include('@Beffroi/account/back.html.twig') }}
    <p>{{ 'archive.explanation'|trans }}</p>
    {# The one refusal this page carries, which crossed the redirection in the session (issue #481). #}
    {% if refusal is not null %}<p data-error="{{ refusal }}">{{ ('archive.' ~ refusal)|trans({minimum: passphrase_minimum}) }}</p>{% endif %}

    {# What the file holds is the chapters it is assembled from, so a kind of fact this provider comes to
       hold about a person is named here by being wired and this page is not edited. #}
    <h2>{{ 'archive.what_it_holds'|trans }}</h2>
    <ul data-chapters="{{ chapters|length }}">
        {% for chapter in chapters %}
            <li data-chapter="{{ chapter }}">{{ ('archive.chapter.' ~ chapter)|trans }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>

    <h2>{{ 'archive.your_request'|trans }}</h2>
    <p data-archive="{{ state }}">{{ ('archive.' ~ state)|trans }}</p>
    {# How long the file this person asks for is kept, read where its state is and not inside the button
       that asks for one. #}
    <p data-archive-kept-for="{{ kept_for_days }}">{{ 'archive.kept_for'|trans({days: kept_for_days}) }}</p>
    {% if state == 'being_built' or state == 'stalled' %}
        <p><time datetime="{{ archive.askedAt|date('c') }}">{{ 'archive.asked_at'|trans({moment: archive.askedAt|beffroi_moment(user)}) }}</time></p>

        {# A request a person can take back, whichever of the two states it is in: one they changed their
           mind about, and one whose build never came back, are one row and one thing to say about it. The
           state with no file says so in the label, there being nothing to delete yet. #}
        <form method="post" action="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account_archive_drop') }}" data-archive-cancel>
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('beffroi_archive_drop') }}">
            <button type="submit">{{ 'archive.cancel'|trans }}</button>
        </form>
    {% elseif state == 'ready' %}
        <p><time datetime="{{ archive.builtAt|date('c') }}">{{ 'archive.built_at'|trans({moment: archive.builtAt|beffroi_moment(user)}) }}</time></p>
        <p><time datetime="{{ archive.expiresAt|date('c') }}">{{ 'archive.expires_at'|trans({moment: archive.expiresAt|beffroi_moment(user)}) }}</time></p>
        <p><a href="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account_archive_file') }}" data-archive-file download>{{ 'archive.download'|trans }}</a></p>

        {# The same file under a passphrase this person chose (issue #483). A POST, because a passphrase
           belongs in a body and never in a query string, and the one form of these pages whose answer is
           not a redirection: its answer is the file, and a passphrase kept to be used after a redirection
           would be a passphrase written to a session. #}
        <form method="post" action="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account_archive_wrapped_file') }}" data-archive-wrap="{{ container }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('beffroi_archive_wrap') }}">
            <p>{{ 'archive.wrapped_explanation'|trans({minimum: passphrase_minimum, container: container}) }}</p>
            <label for="archive-passphrase">{{ 'archive.passphrase'|trans }}</label>
            <input type="password" id="archive-passphrase" name="password" minlength="{{ passphrase_minimum }}" autocomplete="new-password" required>
            <button type="submit">{{ 'archive.download_wrapped'|trans }}</button>
        </form>

        {# The file they have is a file this provider stops holding when they say so (issue #453). A week
           is how long it would stay by itself, and nobody has to wait it out: the row goes, and the page
           says again what asking for one would give them. #}
        <form method="post" action="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account_archive_drop') }}" data-archive-drop>
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('beffroi_archive_drop') }}">
            <p>{{ 'archive.drop_explanation'|trans }}</p>
            <button type="submit">{{ 'archive.drop'|trans }}</button>
        </form>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
